  { q: "What is DNS propagation and how do I check it?", a: "DNS propagation is the window after you change a record during which different resolvers around the world still return a mix of old and new answers, governed by TTL and resolver cache state. To check it, query the same record across many public resolvers and look for disagreement. Ollagraph's POST /v1/intel/dns-propagation does exactly this — it queries one record across N public resolvers and reports how consistent the answers are." },
